From: project_alpha contributors
Subject: [PATCH] mingw-w64: use the toolchain's gethostname, snprintf, asprintf

mingw-w64 declares gethostname(char *, int) in winsock2.h, ships a C99
snprintf and declares asprintf/vasprintf in stdio.h. The MSVC/Xbox-era
replacements in compat.h and asprintf.h therefore break the build
("conflicting types for 'gethostname'", "redefinition of 'vasprintf'") and
would map snprintf to the non-terminating _snprintf. Keep them for MSVC and
Xbox only.

Needed for the windows-x86_64 target of tools/libsmb2 (NET-002).
Upstream: not sent yet.
---
 lib/compat.h  | 2 +-
 lib/libsmb2.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/compat.h b/lib/compat.h
--- a/lib/compat.h
+++ b/lib/compat.h
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@
 #define EBADF WSAENOTSOCK
 #endif

-#if defined(_XBOX) || defined(__MINGW32__)
+#if defined(_XBOX)
 #define snprintf _snprintf
 int gethostname(char* name, size_t len);
 #endif
diff --git a/lib/libsmb2.c b/lib/libsmb2.c
--- a/lib/libsmb2.c
+++ b/lib/libsmb2.c
@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@
 #include <sys/socket.h>
 #endif

-#if defined(_WIN32) || defined(_XBOX) || defined(__AROS__)
+#if (defined(_WIN32) && !defined(__MINGW32__)) || defined(_XBOX) || defined(__AROS__)
 #include "asprintf.h"
 #endif

